dotengine/godot/pull/121465#pullrequestreview-4725301061","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121465","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121465#pullrequestreview-4725301061"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121465"}},"submitted_at":"2026-07-17T18:50:25Z","commit_id":"04f3144e39dff44010042bf0c63249e62cf3f6f8"},{"id":4739431777,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGn39YQ","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally (`deprecated=no` build), it works as expected. Code looks good to me.\r\n\r\nI remember discussing the addition of new methods that return enum-based values at some point (to speed up checks, get autocompletion and avoid typos), but we decided it wasn't critical and it was best to continue with the current string-based API. There were also concerns that third-party changes could add new drivers and renderers (with no way to add themselves to the enum), but with what's already available in Godot as of 4.7, it's unlikely to be the case now (except in private forks).\r\n\r\nIf we could expose String constants in the OS class, we could look into doing that in the future for GDScript at least (and C# if it's supported there). For example, `OS.RENDERING_DRIVER_VULKAN_STRING` would be equal to `vulkan`.","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121465#pullrequestreview-4739431777","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121465","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121465#pullrequestreview-4739431777"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121465"}},"submitted_at":"2026-07-20T22:26:22Z","commit_id":"04f3144e39dff44010042bf0c63249e62cf3f6f8"}]